  "application_type_full": "Full planning & display of advertisements",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed communications hub, by reason of its excessive scale, prominent siting, illuminated digital advertising display and proximity to existing street furniture, including the adjacent bus shelter, would result in an incongruous and visually intrusive form of development that would contribute to the proliferation of street clutter and advertisements, harmful to the character and appearance of the streetscene and the visual amenity of the area. The proposal is therefore contrary to adopted Local Plan policy CC1, CC2 and CC5, and the objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed illuminated digital advertisement, by reason of its inappropriate siting in close proximity to a busy bus stop, would fail to provide the minimum clear footway width sought by Transport for London Streetscape Guidance and, given its proximity to West Thames College Bus Stop G, would impede pedestrian movement and compromise accessibility and the safe boarding and alighting of passengers, including wheelchair users and those with pushchairs. The proposal is therefore contrary to adopted Local Plan policy CC5 and EC2, and the objectives of the National Planning Policy Framework."
  ],
